WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.540
In this video, we introduce the features and usage of Antigravity Script Runner

2
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.180
Inside our project structure and File Explorer

3
00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.980
there are usually many different types of files and automation scripts

4
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.400
However in the native VS Code context menu

5
00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:20.280
there is no option to directly run batch files or PowerShell scripts

6
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.800
At the same time, it lacks an intuitive way to preview multimedia files

7
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.880
unable to quickly preview images

8
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:28.540
listen to audio, or play videos directly

9
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:34.240
For creators constantly dealing with media assets and script workflows

10
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:36.440
these are essential and critical requirements

11
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.740
To solve these operational pain points

12
00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.760
I built this right-click context runner extension

13
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.940
fully overcoming native limitations

14
00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.980
and greatly enhancing the development and creative experience

15
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.460
First is the "1-Click Script Execution" feature

16
00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.840
When selecting a BAT batch file

17
00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:58.820
PS1 script, or Python file in File Explorer, simply right-click

18
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:02.520
and matching execution commands appear automatically in the menu

19
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.440
Eliminating the need to switch to the terminal and type commands manually

20
00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:10.080
right-click any file to run scripts instantly

21
00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.960
greatly streamlining routine automation workflows

22
00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:17.480
The second key feature is "Folder Image Viewer"

23
00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:23.340
When right-clicking an image folder and selecting the viewer

24
00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:28.960
all images are organized into a dedicated viewer panel

25
00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.920
You can hold the right mouse button to pan smoothly across the canvas

26
00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.640
and freely zoom in or out on images

27
00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:40.300
to quickly inspect AI generations and art assets

28
00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:43.440
In addition, it supports image box selection

29
00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:45.420
along with powerful advanced operations

30
00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:48.320
We can copy full paths of selected images with one click

31
00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:52.560
and paste them into AI chat for follow-up editing or analysis

32
00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:55.160
If generated images do not meet expectations

33
00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.440
they can be deleted right here in one click

34
00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.760
